#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "Reviewing the blueprint"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "Most of the blueprint was drafted quickly, and the maintainers accepted it directly, as [LIP-1]{1} allows before 1.0.0. Before anyone builds on it, every part needs a careful reading and a recorded verdict. This guide tells you how that review is organised, what each milestone settles, and how to give a verdict."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "Milestones"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "The review is tracked in the repository's [milestones]{1}. Each one has a due date, which is a target. We move it when the work needs more time, and we say so here when we do."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "The foundations come first because everything else is read against them. The contracts and the domain design can be reviewed side by side. The architecture waits for both, because its diagrams draw the capabilities and the contexts. The guides come last, because they tell you how to apply everything above them."
msgstr ""

