msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "Give a verdict"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "Each area under review has an issue in its milestone, with a checklist of the things to read. Anyone can comment with evidence or a view. The Data Lead and the Technical Lead give the verdict."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "Open the issue and read each item on its checklist."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "Comment with a verdict for each item you have a view on."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "For a page, a principle or a clause, the verdict is **approve**, **change** (give the new wording) or **drop** (give the reason)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "For a decision record, the verdict is **confirm** or **supersede** (say what should replace it). Records are never edited, so a superseded decision gets a new record."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "Make the change the verdict asks for, on the path [CONTRIBUTING]{1} gives it. A change of wording that keeps the meaning is an ordinary reviewed change. A changed or dropped clause, a new domain term, or a superseded decision needs a LIP, which the maintainers may accept straight from Draft until 1.0.0."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "Tick the item once its change has landed, and close the issue when every item is ticked."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/reviewing.md
msgid "If the review turns up something no issue covers, open a new issue in the milestone it affects."
msgstr ""
